// Plan stage R0z Z9c-C (part 4, removed in review round 1: code of a caller spawns the closure of `mid` and pushes to `w` while f reads it (W0405); the program keeps `NESTED_TASK_RUN`, the rule of main).
fn mid(g: fn(fn()), f: fn()) / async { g(|| scope { s => s.spawn(f); () }) }
fn main() / async {
    let w = [1]
    mid(|x| scope { s => s.spawn(x); w.push(3); () }, || print(w.len()))
}
